const FT_SHORT={"AMGN:1": {"f": "Amgen still carries a $2.4B TAVNEOS intangible, about 5.2x the drug's 2025 sales, even though the FDA has proposed withdrawing TAVNEOS, and no call, slide or release states that carrying value.", "i": "A full write-off of the U.S. asset would cut GAAP EPS by about $4.23 a share pre-tax ($3.34 to $3.51 after tax), and withdrawal would remove $459M to $600M of yearly revenue."}, "AMGN:2": {"f": "Amgen's sales deductions rose to 54% of gross product sales in 2025 from 52%, and a $2.2B reserve build, partly put down to \"timing of payments\", gave 2025 operating cash flow about $1.07B of support that can reverse.", "i": "Each extra point of deduction rate costs about $771M of net revenue ($1.42 a share pre-tax), and the excess reserve build is about 10.7% of 2025 operating cash flow."}, "AMGN:3": {"f": "About $84M of TEPEZZA's Q1 2026 growth came from distributor stocking rather than patient demand, though the Q1 call credited demand, and about $62M was still in the channel at the end of Q2.", "i": "The stocking is about 24% of Amgen's $345M of Q1 product-sales growth, a one-quarter growth-quality issue rather than an annual earnings hit."}, "AMGN:4": {"f": "The IRS is seeking at least $7.6B of tax and penalties, before interest, in Amgen's Puerto Rico profit-allocation case.", "i": "$7.6B is about 76% of 2025 operating cash flow, or about $13.97 a share in cash; only the part above Amgen's undisclosed reserve for the case would hit EPS."}, "AMGN:5": {"f": "Amgen's profit-share payments to UCB on EVENITY and to AstraZeneca on TEZSPIRE rose $349M to $1,308M in 2025.", "i": "Profit share rose to 3.7% of product sales from 3.0%, a cost-of-sales drag that management already guides."}, "MRK:1": {"f": "The IRS wants about $1.56B more in transition tax and penalties from Merck, the Q2 2026 10-Q now points toward litigation, and Merck has never mentioned it on a call, release or slide deck.", "i": "About $1.56B of cash plus interest (2.4% of 2025 sales), with a GAAP EPS ceiling of about $0.63 a share; some of it may already sit in Merck's $2.53B tax reserve."}, "MRK:2": {"f": "Merck's inventory that it does not expect to sell within a year rose from $3.8B to $5.9B between December 2024 and June 2026, and kept growing after the tariff risk it was staged for was delayed.", "i": "The long-dated pool is up $2.1B and inventory days rose from 247 to 275 in 2025; the earnings risk beyond the write-downs already guided is not sized."}, "MRK:3": {"f": "Subcutaneous Keytruda has been barred from sale in Germany since December 2025 by a Halozyme injunction, rulings on Germany and seven more European markets are due in late 2026, and management has never raised it.", "i": "Ex-U.S. Keytruda Qlex sales were $68M in Q2 2026 (about $272M a year, 0.4% of sales), so this is a legal catalyst rather than a sized revenue hit."}, "MRK:4": {"f": "Merck's U.S. rebate and chargeback provision fell from $13.3B to $10.0B in 2025, mostly because the Januvia list-price cut shrank gross sales and rebates together.", "i": "The $3.3B fall equals about 5.1% of 2025 sales, but the filings do not show how much of it was a real net-price gain."}, "MRK:5": {"f": "Merck's latest 10-K moved the expected Keytruda IRA price date to January 1, 2029 and says U.S. Keytruda sales will \"decline materially\" after that, stacking IRA pricing on the December 2028 patent expiry.", "i": "U.S. Keytruda sales of $18.8B, 29.0% of 2025 total sales, are exposed to both events; the size of the IRA cut is not disclosed."}, "PFE:1": {"f": "Vyndaqel's share of U.S. ATTR-CM class revenue fell from 74.8% to 50.8% in H1 2026, because the class grew $1,246M while U.S. Vyndaqel stayed flat.", "i": "Vyndaqel took none of the class's growth; against its own 2025 growth rate it is about $161M a half (about $0.32B a year) below trend."}, "PFE:2": {"f": "Pfizer's legal-matters charge doubled to $842M in Q2 2026, and the only settlement dated in the quarter, Depo-Provera, is called \"not material\" in narrower words than the earlier Chantix settlement.", "i": "About $0.148 a share of pre-tax GAAP EPS in Q2 alone; it sits outside adjusted EPS, but settlements are paid in cash."}, "PFE:3": {"f": "Pfizer's contingent consideration liabilities rose to $2,259M in H1 2026 after a $550M fair-value increase tied mainly to the Metsera obesity acquisition.", "i": "A non-cash GAAP charge of about $0.096 a share, outside adjusted EPS; a higher liability also means better odds of hitting the milestones."}, "PFE:4": {"f": "Pfizer's revenue deductions rose from 38.6% to 41.3% of gross product sales in 2025, the Part D redesign hit the CFO flagged in advance, and the rate held at about 40% in H1 2026.", "i": "The 2025 step cost about $2,357M of product revenue against the 2024 rate, with no further widening in 2026."}, "PFE:5": {"f": "Ibrance's Medicare negotiated price of $7,871, 50% below list, starts in 2027, the same year its U.S. basic patent expires.", "i": "At most $1,018M on a list basis (half of $2,036M of Part D gross cost), and less in practice because exclusivity ends the same year."}};
